-- ─── Align the Schema With the Entity Model ─────────────────────────────────────
-- The migrations that shaped most tables after V1 were deleted. An empty database built from V1..V33
-- therefore lacked 153 mapped columns and failed `ddl-auto: validate`; databases created before the
-- deletion already have them.
--
-- Target: the schema existing databases run on (it passes Hibernate validation with the current
-- entities), limited to what the entities map. Sections 1, 2, 6 and 7 are generated by diffing an
-- empty database migrated to V33 against such a database:
--   1. mapped columns the migrations never created, with the running schema's definition
--   2. mapped columns that were stricter than the running schema (NOT NULL, shorter VARCHAR, default)
--   3. payment.order_id type, 4. agreements primary key, 5. stale users.gender CHECK (hand-written)
--   6. legacy baseline columns no entity writes lose NOT NULL, so inserts do not fail
--   7. foreign key, unique and check constraints of the running schema
-- Defaults that are not enum values ('UNKNOWN' for users.gender, 'HOLDING' for escrows.status) are not
-- copied. Apart from section 5, every statement is a no-op on a database that already has this shape.

